1. security:
  run ssh.sh          (hardens ssh by disabling insecure features)
  run ftp.sh          (sets the given users to a scoringusers group and heavily limits perms)
  run ftpfiles.sh    (ftpfilesREVERT.sh if it messes up scoring)
  nobrute.sh        (firewall rules to limit 10 connections per 10s)
    
2. monitoring
  run sshmonitor.sh      (detects active ssh testions)
  additionally sshmonitor2.sh and the two testmonitors    (test modifications of the above)
  users.sh    (prints out list of users not in scoringusers group)
  sshdetect.sh    (prints failed login attempts)
  sshtest and its revert if scoring fucks up   (ssh hardening from sshaudit.com)
  check.sh (chatgpt script to detect sus stuff, 50/50 it does jack shit)  
  checkusers.sh (checks for users outside of the scoringusers list, duplicates in the list, and that sort of stuff)
  
